      {
        "name": "Server IP discrepancy 2026-06-14",
        "type": "concept",
        "descriptions": [
          "docs/databases/<db>.md (for all 9 MediaLogix databases) and dumps/megatron.sql consistently list 20.51.108.231:1433 as the host for Megatron, RedDawn, Prime, EndeavorCentral, MegatronRepository, OutboundFeeds, PetFinder, Trax, and WEB. Independent connection testing in docs/etl/usage-analysis/REPORT.md connects to those databases via 74.179.80.27:1433 (returning @@SERVERNAME = usw2-db-ml-vm-p), while 20.51.108.231:1433 separately returns @@SERVERNAME = CIM-PROD-SQL01 with the Central Inventory database (no Megatron present). Awaits human resolution: either the per-DB docs have a copy-paste error in the Reach line, or there are two routes to the same backend that differ in observable @@SERVERNAME. Surfaced by Merge d757b12 — 2026-06-12 — Alicia Salazar."
        ],
        "origin": "kg_apply_d757b12"
      },
      {
        "name": "usw2-db-ml-vm-p",
        "type": "technology",
        "descriptions": [
          "Azure VM hosting the MediaLogix databases (Megatron, EndeavorCentral, MegatronRepository, OutboundFeeds, PetFinder, Prime, RedDawn, Trax, WEB). Hostname matches the Azure US-West-2 naming convention. Reachable at 74.179.80.27:1433 (SQL Server 2016 SP3). Surfaced 2026-06-14 by the docs/etl/usage-analysis/REPORT.md connection testing; did not appear in any prior wiki / KG / Confluence artifact, consistent with the wiki's documented 'AWS (primary today), Azure (target — active migration underway)' (Confluence-Findings.md line 233)."
        ],
        "origin": "kg_resolve_ip_discrepancy"
      },
      {
        "name": "CIM-PROD-SQL01",
        "type": "technology",
        "descriptions": [
          "Legacy CIM production SQL Server reachable at 20.51.108.231:1433 (SQL Server 2022 CU9). Hosts Central Inventory (vehicles_removed = 40 M rows / 411 GB), ClientInventory, DataOne, Feedhub. The per-database docs Alicia generated 2026-06-11 also reference 20.51.108.231:1433 as the source for the 9 MediaLogix databases, suggesting either (a) the MediaLogix databases co-existed on this host as the legacy source-of-truth before the Azure migration, or (b) Alicia's mssql-scripter used a network route or named instance that reaches the MediaLogix Azure VM via this IP. Resolution pending owner confirmation (Ron Mulder)."
        ],
        "origin": "kg_resolve_ip_discrepancy"
      }
    ],
